#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:6
msgid "Writing a Composable Node (C++)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:10
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:13
msgid "Starting Place"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:15
msgid ""
"Let's assume that you have a regular ``rclcpp::Node`` executable that you "
"want to run in the same process as other nodes to enable more efficient "
"communication."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:17
msgid ""
"We'll start from having a class that directly inherits from ``Node``, and "
"that also has a main method defined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:19
msgid ""
"namespace palomino\n"
"{\n"
"    class VincentDriver : public rclcpp::Node\n"
"    {\n"
"        // ...\n"
"    };\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"int main(int argc, char * argv[])\n"
"{\n"
"    rclcpp::init(argc, argv);\n"
"    rclcpp::spin(std::make_shared<palomino::VincentDriver>());\n"
"    rclcpp::shutdown();\n"
"    return 0;\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:37
msgid "This will typically be compiled as an executable in your Cmake."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:39
msgid ""
"# ...\n"
"add_executable(vincent_driver src/vincent_driver.cpp)\n"
"# ...\n"
"install(TARGETS vincent_driver\n"
"    DESTINATION lib/${PROJECT_NAME}\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:49
msgid "Code Updates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:52
msgid "Add the Package Dependency"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:54
msgid ""
"Your `package.xml <https://github.com/ros2/demos/tree/rolling/composition/"
"package.xml>`__ should have a dependency on ``rclcpp_components``, a la"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:56
msgid "<depend>rclcpp_components</depend>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:60
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can independently add a ``build_depend/exec_depend``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:63
msgid "Class Definition"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:65
msgid ""
"The only change to your class definition that you may have to do is ensure "
"that `the constructor for the class <https://github.com/ros2/demos/tree/"
"rolling/composition/src/talker_component.cpp>`__ takes a ``NodeOptions`` "
"argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:67
msgid ""
"VincentDriver(const rclcpp::NodeOptions & options) : "
"Node(\"vincent_driver\", options)\n"
"{\n"
"  // ...\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:75
msgid "No More Main Method"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:77
msgid "Replace your main method with a ``pluginlib``-style macro invocation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:79
msgid ""
"#include <rclcpp_components/register_node_macro.hpp>\n"
"RCLCPP_COMPONENTS_REGISTER_NODE(palomino::VincentDriver)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:85
msgid ""
"If the main method you are replacing contains a ``MultiThreadedExecutor``, "
"be sure to make note and ensure that your container node is multithreaded. "
"See section below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:89
msgid "CMake Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:90
msgid ""
"First, add ``rclcpp_components`` as a dependency in your CMakeLists.txt with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:92
msgid "find_package(rclcpp_components REQUIRED)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:96
msgid ""
"Second, we're going to replace our ``add_executable`` with a ``add_library`` "
"with a new target name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:98
msgid "add_library(vincent_driver_component SHARED src/vincent_driver.cpp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:102
msgid ""
"Third, replace other build commands that used the old target to act on the "
"new target. Don't forget to add ``rclcpp_components::component`` in "
"``target_link_libraries``. i.e. "
"``target_link_libraries(vincent_driver ...)`` becomes "
"``target_link_libraries(vincent_driver_component rclcpp_components::"
"component ...)``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:106
msgid "Fourth, add a new command to declare your component."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:108
msgid ""
"rclcpp_components_register_node(\n"
"    vincent_driver_component\n"
"    PLUGIN \"palomino::VincentDriver\"\n"
"    EXECUTABLE vincent_driver\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:116
msgid ""
"Fifth and finally, change any installation commands in the CMake that "
"operated on the old target to install the library version instead. For "
"instance, do not install either target into ``lib/${PROJECT_NAME}``. Replace "
"with the library installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:120
msgid ""
"ament_export_targets(export_vincent_driver_component)\n"
"install(TARGETS vincent_driver_component\n"
"        EXPORT export_vincent_driver_component\n"
"        ARCHIVE DESTINATION lib\n"
"        LIBRARY DESTINATION lib\n"
"        RUNTIME DESTINATION bin\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:132
msgid "Running Your Node"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:134
msgid ""
"See the :doc:`Composition tutorial <Composition>` for an in-depth look at "
"composing nodes. The quick and dirty version is that if you had the "
"following in your Python launch file,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:137
msgid ""
"from launch_ros.actions import Node\n"
"\n"
"# ..\n"
"\n"
"ld.add_action(Node(\n"
"    package='palomino',\n"
"    executable='vincent_driver',\n"
"    # ..\n"
"))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:149
msgid "you can replace it with"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:151
msgid ""
"from launch_ros.actions import ComposableNodeContainer\n"
"from launch_ros.descriptions import ComposableNode\n"
"\n"
"# ..\n"
"ld.add_action(ComposableNodeContainer(\n"
"    name='a_buncha_nodes',\n"
"    namespace='',\n"
"    package='rclcpp_components',\n"
"    executable='component_container',\n"
"    composable_node_descriptions=[\n"
"        ComposableNode(\n"
"            package='palomino',\n"
"            plugin='palomino::VincentDriver',\n"
"            name='vincent_driver',\n"
"            # ..\n"
"            extra_arguments=[{'use_intra_process_comms': True}],\n"
"        ),\n"
"    ]\n"
"))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Writing-a-Composable-Node.rst:175
msgid ""
"If you need multi-threading, simply add the ``--executor-type multi-"
"threaded`` argument to your container node."
msgstr ""
